{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>בהררם.</b> On their mountain." "<b>איל פארן.</b> As the Targum renders it: מִישׁוֹר, a plain. And I say that אֵיל does not mean מִישׁוֹר, but rather the plain of Paran — its name is אֵיל; and that of Mamre — its name is אֵלוֹנֵי; and that of the Jordan — its name is כִּכָּר; and that of Shittim — its name is אָבֵל, as in אָבֵל הַשִּׁטִּים; and likewise בַּעַל גָּד — its name is בַּעַל. And all of them are translated מִישׁוֹר, and each one's name is upon it." "<b>על המדבר.</b> Next to the wilderness, as in ״וְעָלָיו מַטֵּה מְנַשֶּׁה״ (Numbers 2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:37.130008667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}